    <data name="LegalPrivacy2Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What we collect</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy2Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>When you join the waitlist: your email address, your first name if you give it, the platforms you chose, your language and the page that brought you here. When you use the chat: your questions, which are sent to an AI provider to be answered and aren't kept after the conversation. With your consent only: how pages load and which ones are read, without cookies and without telling who you are. Always: the errors the site runs into in your browser, without telling who you are, and the server's logs of requests, including IP addresses, kept briefly for security.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy3Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Why we may use it</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy3Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Your consent, for the waitlist and the usage statistics. Our legitimate interest in keeping the site secure and working, for the server's logs and the error reports.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy4Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Who else handles it</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy4Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The companies that host the site, send our emails, answer the chat and store the usage statistics, only on our instructions. We sell no data to anyone.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy5Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>How long we keep it</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy5Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Waitlist details until you unsubscribe or we launch and send the last email. Server logs and error reports for 30 days. Chat questions not at all.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy6Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Your rights</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalPrivacy6Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>You can ask for a copy of your data, have it corrected or deleted, object to its use, and withdraw your consent at any time from the privacy settings in the footer. You can also complain to your data protection authority.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalTermsTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Terms of use</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalTermsLede" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The rules for using this website. The app has terms of its own, shown when you install it.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalTerms1Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Using this site</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalTerms1Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>You may read, share and link to this site. Don't try to break it, overload it or get around its limits, and don't use the chat or the waitlist to send anything unlawful.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalTerms2Title" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What's on it</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalTerms2Body" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>We work to keep it accurate, but prices, dates and features can change before launch, and the chat's answers can be wrong. The app's store page and its own terms are what count.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="LegalTerms3Title" xml:space="preserve">
